==Kikuyu==

===Etymology===
Hinde (1904) records ''hiti'' as an equivalent of English {{m|en|hyæna}} in “Jogowini dialect” of Kikuyu, listing also {{cog|kam|mbiti}} and {{cog|sw|fisi}} together with {{m|sw|pisi}} as its equivalents.<ref name="hh1904">Hinde, Hildegarde (1904). [https://archive.org/details/vocabulariesofka00hindiala ''Vocabularies of the Kamba and Kikuyu languages of East Africa''], pp. 32&ndash;33. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hìtí/|lang=ki}}
: {{ki-tonal classes|3|2-4|del=hiti}}
* {{qualifier|Kiambu}}
:* {{qualifier|Limuru}} {{ki-tonal classes|||latent-H|del=hiti}}

===Noun===
{{ki-noun|9/10|hiti}}

# [[hyena]], especially [[spotted hyena]] (''[[Crocuta crocuta]]'')<ref>Kingdon, Jonathan (1977). ''East African Mammals: An Atlas of Evolution in Africa, [https://books.google.co.jp/books?id=bQjh35ER6ggC&dq=&hl=en&source=gbs_navlinks_s Volume III Part A (Carnivores)]'', p. 260. Chicago: The University of Chicago Press. {{ISBN|0-226-43721-3}}</ref>

====Derived terms====
